<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Darwin, Northern Territory</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Darwin is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s Northern Territory, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> Sea. Founded by South Australia in 1869 as Palmerston, it became the northern end of the Overland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">Telegraph</a> in 1872 and was officially renamed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-darwin">Charles Darwin</a> in 1911. Japanese air raids from February 1942 made it the most heavily bombed place in Australia, and Cyclone Tracy devastated it in 1974.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/darwin-northern-territory.jpg" alt="Darwin, Northern Territory" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagai Agmon-Snir حچاي اچمون-سنير חגי אגמון-שניר · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DarwinOct172024_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
